# macOS/iCloud duplicate artefacts: "foo 2.ts" beside "foo.ts". Three were
# swept into a commit by `git add -A` on 14/10/2026.
#
# ANY extension, because listing them one at a time does not hold. On
# 10/11/2026 "populateApprovedPricingCatalogue.d 2.mts" showed up in
# `git status` for exactly that reason — .mts was not on the list — and
# the next `git add -A` would have committed it. Seventeen of these were
# in the tree that morning, including .png, .wav, .webp, .svg, .html,
# .webmanifest and .js copies in dist/.
#
# Whatever makes them is still running: five appeared in one minute
# while three branches were being merged, every one of them a copy of a
# file that merge had just touched. So the rule has to cover the
# extensions nobody has thought of yet.
#
# Two digits as well as one: "index 3.html" exists, and nothing stops a
# tenth copy.
#
# The SPACE before the digits is what keeps this safe, and it is the
# whole reason the pattern can be this broad:
# scripts/moego-sync-2026-10-12.ts has a hyphen and stays tracked. No
# tracked file in the repository matches, checked before widening it.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*

# MoeGo pulls. Every one is a list of real clients with their phone
# numbers, and this repository is on GitHub. The import script reads
# the file from a path outside the repo for the same reason.
*.tsv
scripts/moego-*.tsv

# Reversal files written by the one-off apply scripts. Operational output
# with client and appointment ids in it, regenerated on every run — it
# belongs on the machine that ran the script, not in the repo.
scripts/out/
